<item><title>Sierra Leone charcoal trade sustains families as tree loss threatens food security</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-charcoal-trade-sustains-families-as-tree-loss-a237a3/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-charcoal-trade-sustains-families-as-tree-loss-a237a3/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>A 65-year-old burner says his family depends on the work, while an environmental agency director warns that producers are cutting orange and mango trees.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:38:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" length="34790" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Sierra Leone analyst says vice presidency has no path to power</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-analyst-says-vice-presidency-has-no-path-to-b42fab/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/sl/sierra-leone-analyst-says-vice-presidency-has-no-path-to-b42fab/</guid><category>Sierra Leone</category><description>Foday M. Daboh argues that successive governments have used the office to balance party interests, leaving vice presidents without a clear route to succession.</description><pubDate>Thu, 19 Nov 2026 09:38:00 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" length="34790" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/sl.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
